Relevant table & column checklist  

• `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`  
  – `id`: CHEMBL identifier → value to show in the final list  
  – `name`: official molecule/ingredient name → string‐match to Keytruda, Vioxx, Premarin, Humira  
  – `tradeNames.list.element`: array of brand names → extra place to look for the four terms  
  – `synonyms.list.element`: array of synonyms → extra place to look for the four terms  
  – `drugType`: small‑molecule, antibody, etc. → must be NOT NULL (“known drug type”) and returned  
  – `blackBoxWarning`: BOOL → must be TRUE  
  – `isApproved`: BOOL → must be TRUE  
  – `hasBeenWithdrawn`: BOOL → returned as “withdrawal status”  

Main conditions  

1. LOWER(name OR tradeName OR synonym) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')  
2. `isApproved` = TRUE  
3. `blackBoxWarning` = TRUE  
4. `drugType` IS NOT NULL  

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Example exploration queries  
(Each is capped with LIMIT 20 and wrapped in back‑ticks for copy/paste)

```sql
-- 1) Quick look: find any molecule whose primary name matches one of the brands
SELECT id, name, drugType, isApproved, blackBoxWarning
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
WHERE LOWER(name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Search inside TRADE NAMES only
SELECT DISTINCT m.id, tn.element AS trade_name, m.drugType
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list) AS tn
WHERE LOWER(tn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Search inside SYNONYMS only
SELECT DISTINCT m.id, sn.element AS synonym, m.drugType
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(m.synonyms.list) AS sn
WHERE LOWER(sn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Union of primary name + trade names + synonyms (all matches)
SELECT DISTINCT id
FROM (
  SELECT id FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
  WHERE LOWER(name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT m.id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
       UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list) AS tn
  WHERE LOWER(tn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT m.id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
       UNNEST(m.synonyms.list) AS sn
  WHERE LOWER(sn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Inspect approval & black‑box flags for the four brands
SELECT id, name, isApproved, blackBoxWarning
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
WHERE LOWER(name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Same as (4) but keep only approved molecules carrying a black box warning
WITH brand_ids AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT id
  FROM (
    SELECT id FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
    WHERE LOWER(name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
    UNION ALL
    SELECT m.id
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
         UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list) AS tn
    WHERE LOWER(tn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
    UNION ALL
    SELECT m.id
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
         UNNEST(m.synonyms.list) AS sn
    WHERE LOWER(sn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  )
)
SELECT m.id, m.name, m.isApproved, m.blackBoxWarning
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
JOIN brand_ids USING(id)
WHERE m.isApproved = TRUE
  AND m.blackBoxWarning = TRUE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Add requirement that drugType is known (NOT NULL)
SELECT m.id, m.name, m.drugType
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
JOIN UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list) AS tn
WHERE LOWER(tn.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  AND m.isApproved = TRUE
  AND m.blackBoxWarning = TRUE
  AND m.drugType IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Pull withdrawal status together with previous filters
SELECT m.id, m.name, m.hasBeenWithdrawn, m.drugType
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
WHERE LOWER(m.name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  AND m.isApproved = TRUE
  AND m.blackBoxWarning = TRUE
  AND m.drugType IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) One‑liner returning the three requested fields for any matching source (name/trade/synonym)
WITH matches AS (
  SELECT id FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
  WHERE LOWER(name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT m.id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
       UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list) AS t
  WHERE LOWER(t.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT m.id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m,
       UNNEST(m.synonyms.list) AS s
  WHERE LOWER(s.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
)
SELECT DISTINCT id AS drug_id,
       drugType AS drug_type,
       hasBeenWithdrawn AS has_been_withdrawn
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule`
WHERE id IN (SELECT DISTINCT id FROM matches)
  AND isApproved = TRUE
  AND blackBoxWarning = TRUE
  AND drugType IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL query (remove LIMIT when you want full answer)
SELECT DISTINCT
       m.id                AS drug_id,
       m.drugType          AS drug_type,
       m.hasBeenWithdrawn  AS withdrawal_status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.molecule` AS m
LEFT JOIN UNNEST(m.tradeNames.list)   AS t ON TRUE
LEFT JOIN UNNEST(m.synonyms.list)     AS s ON TRUE
WHERE (
        LOWER(m.name) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
        OR LOWER(t.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
        OR LOWER(s.element) IN ('keytruda','vioxx','premarin','humira')
      )
  AND m.isApproved = TRUE
  AND m.blackBoxWarning = TRUE
  AND m.drugType IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

Each successive query builds knowledge of the data, ending with #10 that directly satisfies:  
“return drug id, drug type and withdrawal status for approved drugs with a black‐box warning and known drug type among Keytruda, Vioxx, Premarin, Humira.”
